{
  "comment": "Typechecks the Node MCP server under mcp/mcp/. Separate from the browser-targeted tsconfig.json -- the MCP emits HTML as strings and has no DOM dependencies. The rest of mcp/ (construct, catalog, blocks, integrations, recipes and the leaf modules at its root) stays in tsconfig.json's browser pass, which is where it was before the 2026-09-02 move: catalog/surfaces.test.ts side-effect-imports nine DOM elements and construct/codegen-cards.render.test.tsx is Solid JSX, so widening this include to mcp/** would go red on files it was never meant to see.",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ESNext",
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "lib": ["ESNext"],
    "types": ["node"],
    "strict": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "baseUrl": ".",
    // This pass imports `@kitn.ai/ui/schemas` (manifest.ts, tools/reference.ts,
    // reference.test.ts) by its PUBLIC specifier on purpose — the MCP emits that
    // exact string into scaffolded routes. Node/TS resolve it through the package
    // `exports` map to ./dist, so before this mapping existed the pass reported 12
    // errors on any tree that had not been built (5x TS2307 plus 7 cascaded
    // implicit-any/unknown), and was green only after `nx build ui`. A typecheck
    // with a hidden build prerequisite fails confusingly on a fresh clone; the
    // sibling trap is the compiled.css one in CLAUDE.md.
    //
    // ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING, DO NOT SWAP. TS tries each entry and takes the first
    // that exists on disk:
    //   1. ./dist/schemas/index(.d.ts) — the SAME file the `exports` map's `types`
    //      condition hands a consumer. On a built tree (CI, prepublish) this pass
    //      therefore checks against the shipped declarations, not the sources, so
    //      it still catches a .d.ts that does not describe what src does.
    //   2. ./src/schemas/index.ts — fallback for an unbuilt tree only.
    // Pointing at src FIRST is still wrong, but no longer for the reason recorded
    // here before: it makes the BUILT tree resolve to source too, so this pass stops
    // checking the shipped declarations and checks the sources twice instead. It no
    // longer costs an ERROR to do it, so entry 1 is held by that reason alone now,
    // not by a compile failure.
    //
    // Entry 2 IS fully green as of src/primitives/card-component-types.ts. The
    // barrel's public surface used to type-import CardComponentMap from
    // primitives/card-registry.TSX, and this project deliberately has no `jsx`, so an
    // unbuilt tree reported exactly 1 TS6142. CardComponent / CardComponentMap now
    // live in that DOM-free .ts the way the tag half already did, and this pass
    // reports 0 errors with no dist/ present — which is the check that tells the
    // difference, so run it that way. Granting `jsx` instead was re-measured on this
    // tree at 130 errors (838 without `jsxImportSource`); see card-tags.ts for the
    // 1364 figure on the broader case.
    "paths": {
      "@kitn.ai/ui/schemas": ["./dist/schemas/index", "./src/schemas/index"]
    }
  },
  "include": ["mcp/mcp/**/*.ts"]
}
